<title>JAPAN: Moody's rates Eureka floating rate notes Aaa.</title>
<headline>Moody's rates Eureka floating rate notes Aaa.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Monday it had assigned a rating of Aaa to 2.5 billion yen in secured floating rate notes issued out of a Euro medium-term note (MTN) programme by Eureka Finance Ltd (Eureka).</p>
<p>Eureka is a special-purpose company formed in the the Cayman Islands, Moody's said in a statement.</p>
<p>Moody's said the rating is based on a guaranteee provided by Sumitomo Marine &amp; Fire Insurance Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
